2026-05-06T05:35:30.982Z JOY-0163-6B comment.added "Design decided 2026-05-06 (collaborative) - hybrid joy update with implicit auto-sync.\n\nUpdate channel: GitHub Releases via cargo-dist + axoupdater. Stays GitHub for the foreseeable future.\n\nMechanics:\n- New 'joy update' subcommand wraps axoupdater (AxoUpdater::new_for("joy").load_receipt()?.run_sync()?). Receipt-gated, so brew/cargo-install users are skipped gracefully with a clear 'use your installer' message instead of a clobber.\n- After a successful binary swap, joy update runs the in-repo sync: lazy-activation (.gitattributes + merge driver) + the work joy auth update does (SECURITY.md, project.yaml schema) + the work joy ai update does (AI tool files). Output lists each touched file: 'refreshed: SECURITY.md', 'registered: .gitattributes', etc.\n- Per-clone version marker stored in local git config: joy.last-sync-version. Vcs trait gains config_get/config_set so this stays inside the abstraction (ADR-010). Marker is per-clone, lives in .git/config or .git/modules/<sub>/config for submodules.\n- Auto-sync: every joy invocation (on top of the lazy-activation we already have) compares CARGO_PKG_VERSION to joy.last-sync-version. Mismatch -> runs the same sync routine, prints the same 'refreshed: ...' summary, then proceeds with the user's actual command. Symmetric to joy update's Phase-1 output so users don't see surprise dirty files.\n- Toggle for the auto-sync goes into .joy/config.yaml (auto-sync: true|false), with the per-clone marker staying in git config (separation: user preference vs implementation state).\n- Per-domain commands joy ai update + joy auth update become internal routines used by joy update. Public CLI keeps them for one or two release cycles as deprecated aliases, then removes.\n- AI session-start check removed entirely. CLAUDE.md template tells the AI: 'after any joy command, if the output mentions refreshed: CLAUDE.md (or your tool file), re-read it'. The dedicated joy ai update --check at session start goes away because the auto-sync already covers it.\n- Modes: collaborative+ asks before each refresh, autonomous just does it, pairing walks through file by file.\n\nImplementation scoped in JOY-0164 (next item). This rework item closes when that lands and we have field signal that the auto-sync is reliable." [ai:claude@joy delegated-by:horst.schwarz@joydev.com]
2026-05-06T05:44:07.078Z JOY-0164-B5 item.created "Add joy update with axoupdater + auto-sync on every invocation" [ai:claude@joy delegated-by:horst.schwarz@joydev.com]
2026-05-06T07:40:45.363Z JOY-0164-B5 comment.added "[x] axoupdater wired: dist-workspace.toml gets install-updater=true; joy-cli depends on axoupdater 0.10 with the blocking feature.\n[x] joy update subcommand: binary swap via AxoUpdater::run_sync() (receipt-gated, brew/cargo-install builds skip with a clear message). Then runs the in-repo sync.\n[x] joy update --check: reports binary state (receipt missing or up-to-date or update available) and repo state (synced / stale / never-synced). Exit 2 if anything is stale.\n[x] Per-clone version marker in git config: joy.last-sync-version. Helpers init::last_sync_version + init::set_last_sync_version (using GitVcs::config_get/set inherent methods for now).\n[x] Auto-sync hook in main.rs: every joy invocation reasserts lazy-activation, then if auto-sync is enabled and the marker mismatches the current binary version, runs init::run_sync and prints a one-line 'joy X.Y.Z: synced this repo' summary on stderr.\n[x] auto-sync: bool default true added to .joy/config.yaml (Config struct in joy-core/model/config.rs). Snapshot updated.\n[x] 5 bats tests: receipt-missing reporting, repo synced after first invocation, marker stamped on first invocation, stale marker triggers resync output, auto-sync: false in config.yaml is honoured.\n\nDeferred to follow-up items (still under JOY-0163-6B umbrella):\n- Bundling joy auth update + joy ai update into the sync orchestrator (current run_sync only does lazy-activation + stamp marker)\n- Vcs trait extension for config_get/set (today they live as GitVcs inherent methods; ADR-010 wants them on the trait)\n- AI template updates (drop the joy ai update --check session-start ritual, add 'watch for refreshed:' guidance)\n- Deprecation of joy ai update / joy auth update CLI surface" [ai:claude@joy delegated-by:horst.schwarz@joydev.com]
